From 7e903c90192679a8881d1a5ddf6d5be4d5478356 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pugant <pugant@localhost>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 15:14:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] restore-read-once + meta-bulk/bitset: single cold read
 for persist/park restores [w6-5]

W6-5 (A3-1 var.B + A3-4). The persist/park restore used to read the whole
entry payload from disk TWICE: llama_persist_crc32_file for the sidecar
verify (which ends with POSIX_FADV_DONTNEED), then the load pass. load_disk
now streams each component into a host buffer exactly once (CRC folded in
the same pass), verifies both components against the sidecar CRC before
either context is mutated, and restores from RAM via the new
llama_state_seq_load_buffer() - the buffer IO defers backend tensor_set
calls exactly like the proven RAM-restore path. On allocation failure the
two-pass disk path serves the restore unchanged.

A3-4: kv/recurrent state meta now bulk-reads the fixed-size single-seq
record block (one io.read instead of 3-4 per cell) and writes the per-cell
head as one block (seq_ids vector hoisted out of the loop); seq bitset
iteration (seq_pos_rm/add, seq_get) visits only set bits via
_Find_first/_Find_next on libstdc++ (plain scan fallback elsewhere).
Incremental CRC exposed as llama_persist_crc32_folder (pimpl over the
wave-5 crc32_stream).

Gate N: test-state-io-buffer (tiny in-memory model, CPU-only) proves the
buffer restore is bit-identical to the file restore and the on-disk format
unchanged - artifacts byte-identical to the pre-change golden run
(logs/wave6/w6a3-golden-baseline.sha256); test-persist-meta covers the
folder equivalence; new test-kv-cells pins the bitset bookkeeping
(duplicate positions, rm/keep/cp/set transitions).

Gauges unchanged: persist_last_restore_ms / park_restore_crc_ms keep their
meaning (crc_ms = read+verify pass, load_ms = restore), read_path=host-buffer
added to the load marker.

Co-Authored-By: GLM by z.ai
